# `apps/web`

Read `apps/web/README.md` and `apps/web/src/components/ui/README.md` before your
first edit. This file is the compressed version plus the traps.

## 1. Stack — decided, do not substitute

Vite 7 · React 19 · react-router 7 (data-router APIs) · TanStack Query 5 for
server state · Zustand 5 for UI-only state · **Tailwind CSS v4** · shadcn/ui as a
generator · `radix-ui` (the unified package) · CVA + `clsx` + `tailwind-merge` via
`src/lib/cn.ts` · `lucide-react` imported one icon at a time ·
`@tanstack/react-virtual` · Vitest + Testing Library + axe-core.

**Tailwind v4 specifically.** There is no `tailwind.config.js`, no
`postcss.config.js`, and no `@tailwind base/components/utilities`. Configuration is
CSS: `@import 'tailwindcss'` and `@theme inline { … }` in `src/design/tokens.css`,
wired by `@tailwindcss/vite`. If you write any of those three things you have
followed a v3 tutorial — stop and re-read the v4 docs.

**shadcn is a code generator, not a dependency.** It writes a file and exits;
nothing upstream maintains it. Every generated file in `components/ui/` has been
rewritten onto this project's tokens. **Never re-run `shadcn add` over a file in
that directory** — it overwrites, and the retuning is what gets lost.

## 2. The failure that is silent

An unknown Tailwind utility **emits no CSS and fails nothing**. No error, no
warning, no red in CI — the element simply has no style, and on a dark surface a
missing colour often looks plausible.

`tokens.css` deletes Tailwind's default 22-hue palette (`--color-*: initial`), so
`bg-zinc-800`, `text-red-500` and `border-gray-200` are all *silently nothing*.
There is no palette to fall back on. The complete colour vocabulary is:

| Group | Utilities |
| --- | --- |
| Surfaces | `canvas` `surface` `surface-2` `surface-3` `raised` `overlay` |
| Text | `fg` `fg-muted` `fg-subtle` |
| Borders | `border` `border-strong` `border-control` |
| Brand | `primary` `primary-hover` `primary-fg` `primary-accent` `primary-soft` `primary-soft-fg` |
| Inverse | `contrast` `contrast-hover` `contrast-fg` |
| Status | `{success,warning,info,danger}-{accent,solid,fg,soft,soft-fg}`, plus `danger-hover` |
| Neutral | `neutral-solid` `neutral-soft` `neutral-soft-fg` |
| Per-entity | `entity-0`…`entity-7` and `entity-0-fg`…`entity-7-fg` |
| Focus | `ring` |

And the non-colour scales: `rounded-{control,card,panel,window,chip}`;
`shadow-{xs,card,raised,drag,overlay}`; `text-{2xs,xs,sm,base,md,lg,xl,2xl,3xl}`;
`font-{sans,mono}`; the named spacing steps
`{rail,nav,tree,detail,column,topbar,subbar,row,avatar}` (used as `w-rail`,
`h-topbar`, `size-avatar`); `ease-{out,in-out,emphasis}`;
`animate-{fade-in,fade-out,pop-in,pop-out}`.

Need a value that is not there? Add the token to `tokens.css` with its measured
contrast ratio in a comment beside it. Do not reach for an arbitrary value —
eslint rejects a hex in JSX and rejects arbitrary values in colour, spacing,
radius, shadow and type utilities. Layout escapes (`w-`, `h-`, `grid-cols-`,
`inset-`, `z-`, `translate-`) are exempt on purpose: geometry sometimes has no
token and a colour never does.

**A class name Tailwind cannot read as text does not exist.** v4 finds utilities by
scanning source files, so `` className={`bg-entity-${tone}`} `` generates nothing.
Colours indexed at run time come from a literal table — see
`components/data/user-avatar.tsx`. And you cannot make a class exist by writing it
in a test: `tokens.css` carries `@source not '../**/*.test.{ts,tsx}'` precisely so
a test cannot feed the production stylesheet and hide this bug.

## 3. Things that look like bugs and are not

Deleting any of these is silent, and CI goes green.

- **`@ts-expect-error` in a test file is a type pin, not a suppression.**
  `tsc` reports TS2578 the moment the line below one starts compiling — that *is*
  the assertion. `PopoverContent` requiring one of `aria-label`/`aria-labelledby`,
  and `AvatarImage` requiring `alt`, are enforced by nothing else.
- **Tests that assert an absence are load-bearing.** `expect([...el.classList]
  .filter(c => c.startsWith('bg-'))).toEqual([])` is the only check that the
  `outline` variant has no fill.
- **`aria-hidden={false}` on the select marker is deliberate** and was
  negative-tested; the comment says so.
- **Three tsconfigs, and the names matter.** `tsconfig.json` must include every
  file because it is the only project a language server discovers;
  `tsconfig.app.json` is the narrow one proving app code cannot import `node`.
  `conventions.test.ts` fails if either stops holding. Do not merge them.
- **Class order is sorted by machine.** `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss` with
  `tailwindFunctions: ["cn", "cva"]`. The order sometimes reads oddly; it is
  canonical, and class order never decides which rule wins anyway.
- **A tapped arrow key does not change a Radix radio-group's value** in jsdom, only
  its focus — selection needs the key held (`{ArrowDown>}`). Test artifact.
- **`Switch` toggles on Enter and `Checkbox` does not.** Upstream and deliberate.
- **`src/test/dom.ts` patches `Element.prototype.matches`.** It is not paranoia:
  without it the overlay suites take 16.67s and three time out. `dom.test.ts`
  asserts both halves of that.

## 4. Accessibility is a gate, not a pass

`jsx-a11y` violations are eslint **errors**. Target WCAG 2.2 AA, measured rather
than assumed: every colour pair's ratio is recorded beside its token and asserted
in `src/design/contrast.test.ts`. **Change a colour token and that test is your
check** — it will tell you the real measured number, and if a claim in a comment
disagrees with the CSS, the comment is what is wrong.

Query by role and label, never by test id. New interactive surface gets
`expectNoAxeViolations` from `src/test/axe.ts`.

## 5. Boundaries inside the tree

- `fetch` only inside `src/api/`. One `request()`, one error path, every response
  `.parse()`d into a typed `ApiError` or a contract type.
- `stores/` is client state only — panels, selection, theme. Never server data;
  that is TanStack Query's job.
- `routes/` compose. They do not fetch.
- Reuse over duplication. Before writing a component, check `components/ui/` (17
  primitives) and `components/data/` (10 flux-level ones).
